/* book Worked example 2: Q: For the same beam (230 mm × 450 mm effective, M25, Fe415), find the limiting moment of resistance Mu,lim and the steel area that produces it.
   1. xu,max = 0.48 × 450 = 216 mm, the limit for Fe415 from the table.
   2. C = 0.36 × 25 × 230 × 216 = 447,120 N.
   3. z = 450 − 0.42 × 216 = 359.3 mm; Mu,lim = 447,120 × 359.3 = 160.6 × 10⁶ N mm = 160.6 kNm.
   4. Check with the constant: 0.138 × 25 × 230 × 450² = 160.7 kNm.
   5. Ast,lim = C/(0.87fy) = 447,120/361.05 = 1238 mm². More steel than this would push xu past 216 mm.
   Answer: Mu,lim ≈ 160.6 kNm with Ast,lim ≈ 1238 mm²; the beam of the first worked example, at 88.4 kNm, uses a little over half of it. */
